+\section{Related Work}
+\label{sec:related_work}
 
+In this section we review the previous works on Federated HPC, Mathematical Optimization of scheduling problems and Cloud Computing. As MOSPACE addresses centralized scheduling at the federation level, we focus on approaches that coordinate resource allocation across distinct computing infrastructures, as well as optimization methods for scheduling jobs under heterogeneous resource constraints. We first examine existing mechanisms for multi-cluster and federated scheduling, followed by  mathematical formulations for scheduling on heterogeneous machines. Particular attention is given to the extent to which these approaches jointly account for job turnaround, monetary expenditure, resource availability, and data-transfer overheads.
 
 
 
